/* ==========================================================================
 * PL_UNIVERSITIES -- Polish institution directory dataset
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * PROVENANCE -- READ BEFORE EDITING
 *
 * Generated. Do not hand-edit: rebuild with
 *   python3 _tooling/build_dataset_pl.py
 *
 * Every institution here comes from Poland's own two registers. Nothing is
 * invented and the list is not padded.
 *
 *   POL-on / RAD-on -- the Integrated System of Information on Science and
 *   Higher Education, kept by the Minister of Science and Higher Education
 *   https://radon.nauka.gov.pl/opendata/polon/institutions   (836 rows)
 *   https://radon.nauka.gov.pl/opendata/polon/courses        (11,567 rows)
 *     capture: 2026-09-04
 *
 *   MSWiA -- "Lista jednostek prowadzacych studia zatwierdzonych na potrzeby
 *   przyjmowania cudzoziemcow", the Minister of the Interior and
 *   Administration's list of units approved to admit foreigners for studies
 *     137 rows, as at 2026-07-17
 *
 * WHY 227 AND NOT 348
 *
 * Since 1 July 2025 a unit conducting studies must be approved by MSWiA under
 * art. 144 ust. 4 of the Act on Foreigners before it may admit a foreigner for
 * studies, unless art. 144 ust. 5 exempts it (public ACADEMIC universities,
 * military and state-service universities, church universities under a treaty
 * or statute, research institutes). The transitional period for non-public
 * universities ended 30 June 2026. The approval IS the permission -- as CRICOS
 * registration is in Australia -- so a residence permit for studies cannot be
 * granted for a course at a unit that has neither.
 *
 *   348 operating higher education institutions on the register
 *  -106  neither exempt nor approved: real, state-registered universities
 *       that an international student cannot get a permit to attend
 *  -13  permitted but with no study programme the register calls "prowadzone",
 *       which is every Polish seminary and higher theological institute (they
 *       teach inside the churches' own system), plus the Centre for
 *       Postgraduate Medical Education and the dissolved Military Medical Academy
 *  -2  excluded because the card's fixed "Intl. Admits: Yes" would be false:
 *       Wyzsza Szkola Strazy Granicznej (sworn Border Guard officers only) and
 *       Prawoslawne Seminarium Duchowne w Warszawie (formation for clergy)
 *  =227 listed
 *
 * Poland's military and state-service universities are deliberately KEPT: they
 * run civilian degree tracks open to applicants who are not in uniform, which
 * is what the German Verwaltungshochschulen lack.
 *
 * REAL DATA, straight off the registers:
 *   `name`        the registered name, in Polish, exactly as POL-on holds it.
 *   `location`    the registered city and province. Cities keep their Polish
 *                 spelling and diacritics; Warszawa is rendered Warsaw, the one
 *                 settled English exonym. Provinces use the standard English
 *                 forms.
 *   `programmes`  how many study programmes the register currently records as
 *                 "prowadzone" (being conducted) for that institution. A real
 *                 count off the register, like Ireland's -- not a placeholder
 *                 like the UK page's offerRate. It is a BREADTH figure: it says
 *                 how many distinct programmes exist, not how many are taught
 *                 in English, and not how good they are.
 *   `programs`    (no "me") the institution's own largest subject areas, as
 *                 ISCED-F 2013 broad fields derived from the register's field
 *                 code on each of its live programmes. Real data, not a
 *                 descriptor written by hand. The register's own "field
 *                 unknown" code is dropped rather than guessed at.
 *   `type`        the register's two statutory flags (public/non-public/church
 *                 and academic/vocational), with the 10 institutions of the
 *                 Ministry's Excellence Initiative -- Research University
 *                 (IDUB) programme raised to their own group.
 *
 * EDITORIAL, and marked as such:
 *   `alt`         English names, searched but NEVER rendered. POL-on holds no
 *                 English names at all, so for the ranked 20 this is the name QS
 *                 itself prints and for the tail it is derived by rule from the
 *                 Polish name. Without it the directory is unusable for an
 *                 applicant who only knows "Warsaw University of Technology".
 *
 * RANKING
 *   `rank` is a sequential position 1..227. It is meaningful ONLY where
 *   `ranked` is true -- entries 1-20, ordered by their world position in the
 *   QS World University Rankings 2027 (published 18 June 2026), which covers
 *   exactly 20 Polish institutions. Entries 21-227 carry NO ranking meaning:
 *   they are ordered by statutory category and then alphabetically. The UI
 *   prints "#N" only when `ranked` is true and a dash otherwise, so they are
 *   never presented as holding a position.
 *
 *   IDUB is not the same set as the QS-ranked: Gdanski Uniwersytet Medyczny is
 *   an IDUB research university QS does not rank, and Politechnika Krakowska is
 *   QS-ranked and not IDUB.
 * ========================================================================== */
